      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Congenital coronary sinus anomalies are unusual and they rarely coexist with accessory atrio-ventricular pathways. These anomalies are generally symptomatic; however they can cause difficulty in mapping. The association between accessory pathway and coronary sinus anomalies may suggest an embryological link. Here, we report on a male patient with an accessory conducting pathway in the coronary sinus, leading to Wolff-Parkinson-White (WPW) syndrome."},
